The Hessian isn't going to work until Stan 2.5.  I jumped
the gun in announcing that it was done.  The pull request
is:

https://github.com/stan-dev/stan/pull/706

and it's still going through testing.  The full higher-order
derivative tests for all our functions take days to run because
we evaluate every permutation of calls using scalars, vectors,
arrays, and auto-diff or double variables, because the
implementations branch on all these.

We'll add a Hessian method like the gradient method, but you
can already use it through the functionals in

  src/stan/agrad/autodiff.hpp

It just won't autodiff the probability functions until the
patch is merged.

- Bob

