The following should work:

matrix [R, C] bla;

matrix [R, C] orderedbla;

for (r in 1:R) {

  row_vector [C] temp;
  temp <- sort_asc(row(bla, r)); #row function select the rth row of the matrix
  for (c in 1:C) {
    orderedbla[r, c] <- temp[c];
  }
}

Notice that real bla[R, C]; is not a matrix, but an array of two dimensions

