I generated a 1000x2 data matrix where the respective degrees of freedom were 6 and 15. Correlation was 0.25. Here are the relevant output lines:

            Mean     MCSE   StdDev        5%       50%       95%  N_Eff  N_Eff/s    R_hat

nu[1]    4.0e+00  2.4e-04  4.0e-03   4.0e+00   4.0e+00   4.0e+00    268  3.2e-01  1.0e+00

nu[2]    4.0e+00  2.4e-04  3.8e-03   4.0e+00   4.0e+00   4.0e+00    260  3.1e-01  1.0e+00

R_hat is 1 in both cases, so it seems to think it's converged. But in both cases, it's decided that nu=4. That happens to be the lower bound on my prior for nu. This suggests a coding error on my part, but I can't find it. (A modified version of the model for univariate t data properly recovers the degrees of freedom using the same scale mixture representation.)

Ravi

