Hi

Going back for a second to the advice prior for a covariance matrix. In the paper that Andrew pasted it seems that the recommendation of using the wishart distribution is to keep the matrix away of going non-positive. But at the same time Bob explains that the lkj does the same work, in my experience in Stan (as I usually set the model) the lkj seems more straight forward to me.

Is there any substantial benefit of the lkj over the wishart, or over a non-informative (uniform) correlation matrix? Or could they be equivalent?

Thanks for your time

--- Mauricio Garnier-Villarreal

